{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Robustness.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Robustness.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"regression robustness regression robustness","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Robustness.md","fileName":"Regression Robustness.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Regression Robustness","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Regression Model Development]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regression Model Development","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Robustness.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Robustness.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"regression robustness regression robustness","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Robustness.md","fileName":"Regression Robustness.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Regression Robustness","heading":"Regression Robustness","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Regression robustness is the stability of a substantive conclusion across reasonable model specifications, coding choices, and covariate sets. If the exposure estimate remains far from significance or retains a similar magnitude after defensible adjustments, the conclusion is less dependent on one arbitrary formula.\n\nRobustness should be demonstrated with planned sensitivity analyses rather than declared from a single large model. A stable estimate can still be biased when all specifications share the same flawed measurement or selection process.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regression Model Development","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Robustness.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Regression Robustne